 "narrative": "## The trajectory\nRevenue was $31.7B in FY2025 [1].\nRevenue CAGR was +3.8% over FY2016..FY2025 [2].\nNet income was $5.0B in FY2025 [3].\n\n## Growth quality\nRevenue growth in FY2025 was +5.6% [1] [4].\nNet income growth in FY2025 was +9.8% [3] [5].\nIn FY2025, net income growth of +9.8% [3] [5] was above revenue growth of +5.6% [1] [4].\n\n## Margins\nOperating margin was 27.2% in FY2025 [6].\nOperating margin changed +0.8pp in FY2025 [6] [7].\nNet margin was 15.7% in FY2025 [8].\n\n## Cash & balance sheet\nIn FY2025, free cash flow of -$1.7B [9] was below net income of $5.0B [3].\nThe current ratio was 0.55\u00d7 in FY2025 [10], below 1.00\u00d7.\nIn FY2025, operating cash flow of $12.3B [11] was above net income of $5.0B [3].\n\n## Red flags\nLong-term debt grew +75.8% from FY2016 to FY2025. Source operands: Long-term debt USD 45,576,000,000 in FY2016 [12]; Long-term debt USD 80,108,000,000 in FY2025 [13].\nCurrent ratio is below 1.0 (0.55\u00d7 in FY2025). Source operands: Current ratio 0.6960x in FY2016 [14]; Current ratio 0.5518x in FY2025 [10].\n\n## What to watch next\nWatch whether revenue growth in the next reporting update improves from +5.6% in FY2025 [1] [4].\nWatch how operating margin in the next reporting update compares with 27.2% in FY2025 [6].\nWatch how free cash flow in the next reporting update compares with -$1.7B in FY2025 [9].",
